Z||000000||Peachez||10-31-2001||07:43 PM||||I am getting a subwoofer box for the front compartment and need to take off the plastic lining under the spare tire.  I took the bolts off and everything but when i look under the car it looks as if there are a couple bolts to take off down there.  My big problem is the hose on the right that I'm going to have to relocate in order to take the lining off.  I dont wanna screw something up so if anyone has any info about how i should go about this please let me know, i plan to pick up my box this weekend.||||reg||3
Z||000001||tgowens||10-31-2001||11:12 PM||||Peachez, no hoses need to be removed or relocated. There are 7mm hex head screws all the way around the tire well.......when removing it I have found that it is a bit grumpy to get out but best removed from the right front side of the car.......there are no bolts from underneath that need to be removed. It is flexible (to a degree) but it will come out........<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>West Highland Graphics & Design</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Peachez||10-31-2001||11:15 PM||||the plastic lining that i am wondering about is that part that seperates the hood into two pieces.  the hose is on the inside of the compartment.  I believe its the heater hose/vent/blower or whatever you wanna call it.  its sorta wraps around the windshield wiper fluid compartment.  ||||reg||1
